p.append('<h2 id="h">H. Measured performance</h2><p>RTF = generation wall time / playable audio duration. Lower than1 keeps up with playback. SA3 rows exclude already resident worker startup; ACE initialization248.4s included downloads and is not a comparable cold-start benchmark. Memory is process peak RSS; Chestnut tracking is sampled allocation, not verified peak VRAM. Mac unified memory can exceed RSS; ACE caused substantial swap pressure.</p><table><tr><th>Backend / output</th><th>Audio</th><th>Wall</th><th>RTF</th><th>Host peak</th></tr>')
for d in measurements(O):
 duration=d.get('duration',d.get('playable_new_seconds'));wall=d.get('seconds',d.get('generation_seconds'));rtf=wall/duration if duration and wall else None
 if duration and wall:p.append(f'<tr><td>{esc(d["backend"]+" / "+d["sample"])}</td><td>{duration:.2f}s</td><td>{wall:.2f}s</td><td>{rtf:.2f}</td><td>{d.get("host_peak_mib",0):.0f}MiB</td></tr>')
p.append('</table><details><summary>Backend boundaries and exact measurements</summary><pre>'+esc(json.dumps({'backends':inventory(),'measurements':measurements(O)},indent=2))+'</pre></details><p>Source and architecture findings: <a href="../../COMPOSITION.md">COMPOSITION.md</a>. Latest status: <a href="../../STATUS.md">STATUS.md</a>.</p>')
